Comment: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:00.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{=2}===============================DIALOGUE============================
Dialogue: 50,0:01:51.95,0:01:53.03,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,A snake!
Dialogue: 50,0:01:54.37,0:01:55.87,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Wait just a minute.
Dialogue: 50,0:01:55.87,0:01:58.12,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Hey! Kalgara! Look at this!
Dialogue: 50,0:01:59.87,0:02:01.12,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,What a shock.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:01.12,0:02:04.33,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I didn't realize that\Nsnake had a grandchild.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:04.65,0:02:06.44,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,"That snake," huh?
Dialogue: 50,0:02:08.38,0:02:09.80,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,A snake!
Dialogue: 50,0:02:10.78,0:02:11.78,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,{\q2}– Huh?\N– Huh?
Dialogue: 50,0:02:13.54,0:02:15.04,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Would you look at that?
Dialogue: 50,0:02:15.04,0:02:16.91,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It doesn't make any sense.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:16.91,0:02:19.75,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Those two were trying' to kill\Neach other not too long ago.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:19.75,0:02:21.79,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Now they're laughing\Ntogether like good friends.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:22.09,0:02:25.30,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Usually Kalgara isn't very\Nfriendly with the villagers either.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:27.25,0:02:29.75,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I've never seen\Nhim smile like that before.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:31.96,0:02:33.97,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,All right, follow me.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:34.59,0:02:36.13,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,We climb down here.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:36.13,0:02:37.26,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Climb down?
Dialogue: 50,0:02:49.69,0:02:51.53,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,That... ringing.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:52.09,0:02:53.30,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Kalgara.
Dialogue: 50,0:02:53.30,0:02:56.06,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Where is that beautiful\Nringing coming from?
Dialogue: 50,0:02:56.06,0:02:57.97,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Follow me and I will show you.
Dialogue: 50,0:03:35.64,0:03:36.77,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,They're here!
Dialogue: 50,0:03:37.82,0:03:40.16,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You're speechless. I'm not surprised.
Dialogue: 50,0:03:40.92,0:03:42.54,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,This is Shandora.
Dialogue: 50,0:03:42.54,0:03:45.26,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And we're the survivors\Nof this golden city.
Dialogue: 50,0:03:45.37,0:03:47.37,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,A city of gold.
Dialogue: 50,0:03:47.92,0:03:50.88,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It's like I'm dreaming!
Dialogue: 50,0:03:51.09,0:03:54.80,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It's a city... full of treasure!
Dialogue: 50,0:03:54.80,0:03:56.85,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,There's gold everywhere!
Dialogue: 50,0:03:57.48,0:03:58.44,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 50,0:03:59.14,0:04:01.85,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Wait! Everyone stop!
Dialogue: 50,0:04:01.85,0:04:03.14,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It's all right.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:03.14,0:04:05.73,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Load up your ship with\Nall the treasure you can.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:05.73,0:04:07.80,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Just leave the golden bell.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:09.89,0:04:12.68,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,All the villagers here\Nagree that this is right.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:12.68,0:04:13.85,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It is a gift.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:13.85,0:04:16.80,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,We want to thank you for saving our\Ntribe from that terrible disease.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:16.80,0:04:18.30,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,– This is nothing at all.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:18.30,0:04:19.88,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You're so generous, Great Warrior!
Dialogue: 50,0:04:21.36,0:04:23.22,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,But... I don't understand.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:23.22,0:04:26.16,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Haven't your people been working\Nhard to protect this city?
Dialogue: 50,0:04:26.16,0:04:27.28,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,That's true.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:27.28,0:04:29.83,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,We have worked hard to protect it.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:29.83,0:04:31.33,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Although...
Dialogue: 50,0:04:31.33,0:04:34.33,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It's not necessarily\Nthe treasure we guard.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:34.33,0:04:36.08,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Come!
Dialogue: 50,0:04:36.08,0:04:37.37,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Let me show you.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:38.67,0:04:41.09,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,{\q2}– Ah...!\N– Ah...!
Dialogue: 50,0:04:44.28,0:04:46.70,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,The only thing we guard is this stone.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:48.79,0:04:50.16,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Look at that writing.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:51.25,0:04:53.08,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,What's it mean?
Dialogue: 50,0:04:53.08,0:04:54.42,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,We don't know.
Dialogue: 50,0:04:55.42,0:05:00.26,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It is a Poneglyph: writings\Nleft over from ancient history.
Dialogue: 50,0:05:00.26,0:05:03.43,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You mean this isn't something that\Nwas written by your ancestors?
Dialogue: 50,0:05:04.69,0:05:06.90,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,There is only one\Nthing we know for sure.
Dialogue: 50,0:05:06.90,0:05:09.40,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,That the city of Shandora\Nfought and fell trying
Dialogue: 50,0:05:09.40,0:05:11.84,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,to protect this stone,\Nand we will, too.
Dialogue: 50,0:05:11.84,0:05:14.34,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,As descendants, we feel\Nit is our duty to continue
Dialogue: 50,0:05:14.34,0:05:16.65,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,to protect it with the same resolve.
Dialogue: 50,0:05:16.65,0:05:19.78,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,This stone now represents\Nproof that our ancestors
Dialogue: 50,0:05:19.78,0:05:24.49,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,not only fought a\Nvicious fight, but survived.
Dialogue: 50,0:05:24.49,0:05:27.87,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And we revere our ancestors\Nas we would our gods.
Dialogue: 50,0:05:27.87,0:05:33.50,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,{\q2}Still, when I heard the bell ringing before,\NI had no idea it would be this huge.
Dialogue: 50,0:05:35.60,0:05:38.57,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,The bell's rings have words to them.
Dialogue: 50,0:05:38.57,0:05:39.98,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Words?
Dialogue: 50,0:05:39.98,0:05:41.20,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 50,0:05:41.20,0:05:43.45,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It speaks so that the\Nspirits of our ancestors
Dialogue: 50,0:05:43.45,0:05:49.50,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,{\q2}who have passed can still return to this\Nland at any time without getting lost.
Dialogue: 50,0:05:49.50,0:05:52.41,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,We continue to ring the bell\Nas if to shout to them,
Dialogue: 50,0:05:52.41,0:05:57.26,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,"We are here!" "Come home!"\N"We are waiting for you!"
Dialogue: 50,0:05:57.26,0:05:58.64,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And the sound.
Dialogue: 50,0:05:58.64,0:06:02.48,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,The sound itself proclaims\Nthe glory of Shandora.
Dialogue: 50,0:06:02.51,0:06:06.10,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Making its existence known\Nto the ends of the sea!
Dialogue: 50,0:06:06.10,0:06:09.22,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It shouts: "We will never run or hide!"
Dialogue: 50,0:06:10.03,0:06:12.89,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Because of this, we have\Ngiven the grand bell a name.
Dialogue: 50,0:06:12.89,0:06:15.46,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,We call it the "Fire of Shandora."
Dialogue: 50,0:06:15.46,0:06:16.76,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Makes sense.
Dialogue: 50,0:06:16.76,0:06:19.09,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,That explains the majestic sound!
Dialogue: 50,0:06:19.09,0:06:19.90,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You think so?
Dialogue: 50,0:06:20.36,0:06:21.44,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Yeah!
Dialogue: 50,0:06:22.65,0:06:26.84,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It was this fire that reached out\Nto us and helped us arrive here.
Dialogue: 50,0:06:27.73,0:06:31.80,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I heard the ringing\Nduring a terrible storm.
Dialogue: 50,0:06:31.80,0:06:35.47,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I heard it clearly when it\Nshouldn't have been audible at all.
Dialogue: 50,0:06:39.68,0:06:41.95,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You like the bell's ringing too?
Dialogue: 50,0:06:41.95,0:06:43.58,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I bet you do.
Dialogue: 50,0:06:43.58,0:06:48.99,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I bet someday, you'll grow up\Njust like that other giant snake.
Dialogue: 50,0:06:53.04,0:06:55.54,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,But probably not for\Nanother hundred years!
Dialogue: 50,0:06:58.25,0:07:00.71,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Noland, I invite you to stay here.
Dialogue: 50,0:07:00.71,0:07:01.88,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 50,0:07:01.88,0:07:04.49,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It's been 400 years\Nsince Shandora fell.
Dialogue: 50,0:07:04.49,0:07:07.66,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And you're the first guests we've\Nhad, so I want to welcome you.
Dialogue: 50,0:07:07.66,0:07:09.41,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Won't you accept my offer?
Dialogue: 50,0:07:11.40,0:07:12.90,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Kalgara.
Dialogue: 50,0:07:12.90,0:07:15.20,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And with your permission I\Nwould also love the opportunity
Dialogue: 50,0:07:15.20,0:07:17.00,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,to collect some plants from the forest
Dialogue: 50,0:07:17.00,0:07:18.87,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,and see this plague\Nall the way through.
Dialogue: 50,0:07:19.67,0:07:20.76,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Commodore!
Dialogue: 50,0:07:20.76,0:07:22.07,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Commodore!
Dialogue: 50,0:07:22.07,0:07:23.32,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Hold on, now.
Dialogue: 50,0:07:23.32,0:07:24.49,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,What's with the clothes?
Dialogue: 50,0:07:24.49,0:07:26.08,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,We found an Eternal Compass!
Dialogue: 50,0:07:26.08,0:07:27.54,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And look at this map, Commodore!
Dialogue: 50,0:07:27.54,0:07:29.16,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Just look!
Dialogue: 50,0:07:29.16,0:07:32.79,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,We took these items\Nfrom those who intruded upon us.
Dialogue: 50,0:07:32.79,0:07:34.00,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 50,0:07:34.00,0:07:36.75,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,That skull shape is\Ndefinitely our island.
Dialogue: 50,0:07:36.75,0:07:40.76,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,The name "Shandora" means\N"the skull's right eye."
Dialogue: 50,0:07:40.76,0:07:43.13,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,The name refers to the city's location.
Dialogue: 50,0:07:43.13,0:07:44.30,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Right here.
Dialogue: 50,0:07:47.20,0:07:48.91,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Well, take care!
Dialogue: 50,0:07:48.91,0:07:51.58,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And make sure she\Ngets plenty of rest, okay?
Dialogue: 50,0:07:51.58,0:07:53.91,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I will, thanks! G'bye doctor!
Dialogue: 50,0:07:56.52,0:07:57.73,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Hey, look, everyone!
Dialogue: 50,0:07:57.73,0:07:59.69,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Noland brought us some exotic crops!
Dialogue: 50,0:08:01.54,0:08:06.59,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I have a greenhouse on our ship\Nwith all kinds of plant samples.
Dialogue: 50,0:08:06.59,0:08:09.84,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I'll leave some seeds and sprouts\Nhere that are suited for your soil.
Dialogue: 50,0:08:10.22,0:08:11.72,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Does it taste good?
Dialogue: 50,0:08:11.72,0:08:12.64,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Very!
Dialogue: 50,0:08:12.64,0:08:14.22,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And it's full of nutrients!
Dialogue: 50,0:09:15.66,0:09:16.82,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,All right!
Dialogue: 50,0:09:16.82,0:09:19.24,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Time to begin another day of hard work!
Dialogue: 50,0:09:19.24,0:09:20.74,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Hard work doing what?
Dialogue: 50,0:09:20.74,0:09:22.29,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Having a campfire party?
Dialogue: 50,0:09:31.46,0:09:32.67,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,But why?
Dialogue: 50,0:09:32.67,0:09:35.63,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Why would the doctor\Nand the others do this?
Dialogue: 50,0:09:40.25,0:09:41.41,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Chief!
Dialogue: 50,0:09:41.41,0:09:42.74,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Noland and the others are coming!
Dialogue: 50,0:09:43.99,0:09:46.49,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You are not to say\Nanything about last night!
Dialogue: 50,0:09:46.49,0:09:47.83,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Is that clear?
Dialogue: 50,0:09:47.83,0:09:50.79,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,They said they are going\Nto set sail in a few days.
Dialogue: 50,0:09:50.79,0:09:54.06,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,So until then, don't do anything rash.
Dialogue: 50,0:09:54.06,0:09:55.56,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Do you hear me?
Dialogue: 50,0:09:55.56,0:09:57.94,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Fine, then. Our people will\Nnever understand each other.
Dialogue: 50,0:09:57.94,0:09:59.69,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,They've only done harm.
Dialogue: 50,0:09:59.69,0:10:01.61,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I don't care how good his medicine is.
Dialogue: 50,0:10:01.61,0:10:03.07,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,He's still a god killer!
Dialogue: 50,0:10:04.53,0:10:08.07,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,{\q2}Do these people think they can just show\Nup here and stomp all over our history?
Dialogue: 50,0:10:08.07,0:10:09.17,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,They'll pay!
Dialogue: 50,0:10:09.53,0:10:14.58,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,We must endure it, and we must\Nwait quietly for them to leave.
Dialogue: 50,0:10:14.58,0:10:15.62,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,They're here!
Dialogue: 50,0:10:18.46,0:10:19.96,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Hello, everyone.
Dialogue: 50,0:10:19.96,0:10:21.75,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I'm looking for Kalgara.
Dialogue: 50,0:10:30.47,0:10:32.76,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Why is everyone\Nacting so cold all of a sudden?
Dialogue: 50,0:10:32.76,0:10:34.63,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And where's Kalgara?
Dialogue: 50,0:10:34.63,0:10:37.50,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Turn around and leave now.\NYou're not welcome.
Dialogue: 50,0:10:37.50,0:10:39.05,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You're outsiders.
Dialogue: 50,0:10:39.05,0:10:40.86,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Kalgara doesn't want\Nto see you anymore.
Dialogue: 50,0:10:41.37,0:10:42.29,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Seto, stop!
Dialogue: 50,0:10:45.05,0:10:47.32,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,When are you going to leave, anyway?
Dialogue: 50,0:10:47.32,0:10:48.53,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Answer me!
Dialogue: 50,0:10:50.74,0:10:52.24,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 50,0:10:52.24,0:10:54.12,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It seems like they suddenly hate us.
Dialogue: 50,0:10:55.49,0:10:56.62,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Now, hold on!
Dialogue: 50,0:10:56.62,0:10:58.33,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You can't just start acting like this!
Dialogue: 50,0:10:58.33,0:10:59.84,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It's not fair!
Dialogue: 50,0:10:59.84,0:11:00.93,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Let it go.
Dialogue: 50,0:11:02.71,0:11:04.38,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Let's continue our work.
Dialogue: 50,0:11:06.60,0:11:08.73,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,We still have some forest to inspect.
Dialogue: 50,0:11:11.69,0:11:12.99,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,There you are, Kalgara!
Dialogue: 50,0:11:12.99,0:11:15.12,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Noland has been looking for you!
Dialogue: 50,0:11:15.12,0:11:16.45,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I know he has.
Dialogue: 50,0:11:16.45,0:11:19.98,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I have no desire to speak to him.
Dialogue: 50,0:11:19.98,0:11:24.78,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,If I see him right now,\NI'm afraid I might kill him.
Dialogue: 50,0:11:30.70,0:11:31.70,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,That's strange.
Dialogue: 50,0:11:31.70,0:11:33.27,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,The bell didn't ring today.
Dialogue: 50,0:11:33.38,0:11:34.26,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 50,0:11:34.61,0:11:36.98,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It's the first time that's happened\Nin the month that we've been here.
Dialogue: 50,0:11:38.89,0:11:40.30,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Commodore?
Dialogue: 50,0:11:40.46,0:11:43.46,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I'll be done exploring\Nthe forest in two days.
Dialogue: 50,0:11:43.46,0:11:44.28,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Uh... Right.
Dialogue: 50,0:11:44.28,0:11:46.99,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Let everyone know\Nwe set sail in three days.
Dialogue: 50,0:11:47.74,0:11:51.89,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Tell them that this is their last\Nchance to enjoy dry land for a while.
Dialogue: 50,0:11:55.04,0:11:59.29,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,{\q2}Commodore, to tell you the truth,\NI can't wait to get off this insane island.
Dialogue: 50,0:11:59.29,0:12:01.85,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Only after we've finished our duties.
Dialogue: 50,0:12:01.85,0:12:02.97,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Goodnight.
Dialogue: 50,0:12:04.97,0:12:06.90,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,You should stay here, Noland!
Dialogue: 50,0:12:06.90,0:12:08.24,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,I have an idea!
Dialogue: 50,0:12:08.24,0:12:10.23,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,Why don't you make Mousse your wife?
Dialogue: 50,0:12:11.44,0:12:12.77,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,Don't be silly!
Dialogue: 50,0:12:12.77,0:12:15.61,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,I have a family at home\Nand kids who are her age!
Dialogue: 50,0:12:16.62,0:12:18.20,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,You're outsiders.
Dialogue: 50,0:12:18.20,0:12:21.37,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,Kalgara doesn't want\Nto see you anymore.
Dialogue: 50,0:12:21.37,0:12:23.63,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,When are you going to leave, anyway?
Dialogue: 50,0:12:23.63,0:12:24.84,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,Answer me!
Dialogue: 50,0:12:30.40,0:12:32.48,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I know you're here, Kalgara!
Dialogue: 50,0:12:32.48,0:12:34.57,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Come out, now!
Dialogue: 50,0:12:34.57,0:12:38.03,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I won't understand what's\Ngoing on unless you talk to me!
Dialogue: 50,0:12:38.03,0:12:39.61,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,This is ridiculous!
Dialogue: 50,0:12:39.61,0:12:41.16,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Not to mention unfair!
Dialogue: 50,0:12:41.16,0:12:42.20,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 50,0:12:42.20,0:12:44.95,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Come on! We set sail in a few days!
Dialogue: 50,0:12:45.04,0:12:47.62,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I don't want us to part like this!
Dialogue: 50,0:13:01.01,0:13:03.89,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,How dare you show your face here!
Dialogue: 50,0:13:03.89,0:13:06.68,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Do you want your wife\Nto live her life as a widow?
Dialogue: 50,0:13:11.19,0:13:12.65,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Kalgara!
Dialogue: 50,0:13:16.73,0:13:19.61,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,The commodore seems sad lately.
Dialogue: 50,0:13:20.15,0:13:22.53,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Yeah. It's unfortunate.
Dialogue: 50,0:13:22.53,0:13:24.78,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,He thought he made such\Na good friend out here.
Dialogue: 50,0:13:27.79,0:13:30.16,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,None of this makes any sense.
Dialogue: 50,0:13:30.16,0:13:34.17,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It looks like we're gonna set\Nsail first thing tomorrow morning.
Dialogue: 50,0:13:34.17,0:13:37.05,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,The villagers are so upset\Nthat we can't go near them.
Dialogue: 50,0:13:37.36,0:13:40.44,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Plus, I don't remember ever\Nhearing the bell ring today.
Dialogue: 50,0:13:44.07,0:13:46.87,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,How dare you show your face here!
Dialogue: 50,0:13:46.87,0:13:49.79,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,Do you want your wife to\Nlive her life as a widow?
Dialogue: 50,0:14:05.78,0:14:08.99,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I gotta say, this is\Ndefinitely a tough way to leave.
Dialogue: 50,0:14:10.54,0:14:11.50,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Doctor?
Dialogue: 50,0:14:16.29,0:14:18.13,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Good evening.
Dialogue: 50,0:14:18.13,0:14:19.63,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Mousse?
Dialogue: 50,0:14:19.63,0:14:21.59,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Sorry. May I speak with you?
Dialogue: 50,0:14:26.53,0:14:27.61,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Idiot!
Dialogue: 50,0:14:27.61,0:14:29.74,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Why did I believe he was a botanist?
Dialogue: 50,0:14:35.80,0:14:37.72,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Damn you, Noland!
Dialogue: 50,0:14:38.19,0:14:42.15,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,If these are the unfortunate\Nvictims of your advancement,
Dialogue: 50,0:14:42.43,0:14:46.68,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,then we never should have accepted\Nyou or trusted you the way we did.
Dialogue: 50,0:14:50.27,0:14:52.40,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Kindred Trees?
Dialogue: 50,0:14:52.40,0:14:54.15,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 50,0:14:54.15,0:14:56.77,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,We've been told that\Nthe spirits of our ancestors
Dialogue: 50,0:14:56.77,0:14:59.03,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,who died on this island are guided back
Dialogue: 50,0:14:59.03,0:15:02.64,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,by the sound of a bell so\Nthat they may rest inside them.
Dialogue: 50,0:15:02.64,0:15:05.56,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Since the age of Shandora,\Nevery one of our ancestors
Dialogue: 50,0:15:05.56,0:15:08.22,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,who lived on the island\Nwatches over us.
Dialogue: 50,0:15:08.22,0:15:12.23,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,They watch over us from\Nthose sacred, white trees.
Dialogue: 50,0:15:12.23,0:15:15.91,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,That is why the Kindred Wood is\Nso important to us Shandorians.
Dialogue: 50,0:15:19.83,0:15:24.83,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,That is why we've protected them\Nas we've protected our own lives.
Dialogue: 50,0:15:24.83,0:15:28.62,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It's more than just a forest;\Nit's our history.
Dialogue: 50,0:15:28.62,0:15:32.59,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Can you see now why\Nwe hold these trees sacred?
Dialogue: 50,0:15:32.59,0:15:34.68,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And we just chopped them all down.
Dialogue: 50,0:15:36.26,0:15:38.64,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,The warriors felt so betrayed and angry
Dialogue: 50,0:15:38.64,0:15:41.18,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,they grabbed their weapons\Nin search of revenge.
Dialogue: 50,0:15:41.18,0:15:42.81,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,We must drive them off this island!
Dialogue: 50,0:15:42.81,0:15:44.31,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,{\q2}– Yeah! All right!\N– Yeah! All right!
Dialogue: 50,0:15:47.07,0:15:51.64,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,But because you had already saved so\Nmany lives here, they couldn't just...
Dialogue: 50,0:15:53.68,0:15:54.98,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I understand.
Dialogue: 50,0:15:56.27,0:16:00.02,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,They were so grateful\Nthat they couldn't act on it.
Dialogue: 50,0:16:00.02,0:16:03.73,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,But Doctor, even if it\Nwas just for tree research.
Dialogue: 50,0:16:03.73,0:16:05.90,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Even if you didn't know.
Dialogue: 50,0:16:05.90,0:16:08.74,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,The villager's anger won't go away.
Dialogue: 50,0:16:08.74,0:16:11.58,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,So before you go, I thought I'd ask.
Dialogue: 50,0:16:14.66,0:16:16.66,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I have to know the reason why.
Dialogue: 50,0:16:20.26,0:16:23.27,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,So their ancestors'\Nspirits are in those trees?
Dialogue: 50,0:16:23.27,0:16:24.94,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I can't believe I didn't know.
Dialogue: 50,0:16:24.94,0:16:28.44,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And now we've done something\Nterrible that we can't reverse.
Dialogue: 50,0:16:28.44,0:16:31.11,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,They have every right\Nto be as angry as they are.
Dialogue: 50,0:16:31.11,0:16:33.28,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,But Commodore. We had no choice...
Dialogue: 50,0:16:33.28,0:16:35.53,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,There are no excuses!
Dialogue: 50,0:16:35.53,0:16:39.65,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I was too wrapped up in my own\Ninterests to even consider theirs.
Dialogue: 50,0:16:41.99,0:16:46.24,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I was told that besides\Nproclaiming the city's existence,
Dialogue: 50,0:16:46.24,0:16:51.59,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,the bell also served as a guide for\Ntheir ancestors to return to the island.
Dialogue: 50,0:16:52.80,0:16:55.12,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And we just cut them down!
Dialogue: 50,0:16:55.12,0:16:57.95,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,We do not deserve their forgiveness.
Dialogue: 50,0:16:57.95,0:16:59.58,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Commodore, wait.
Dialogue: 50,0:17:02.46,0:17:04.42,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Listen up, everyone!
Dialogue: 50,0:17:04.79,0:17:05.54,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,{\q2}– Huh?!\N– Huh?!
Dialogue: 50,0:17:05.54,0:17:08.18,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You want us to leave\Nthe treasure behind?!
Dialogue: 50,0:17:10.84,0:17:14.18,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I just found out Noland and his\Nmen are getting ready to leave.
Dialogue: 50,0:17:23.14,0:17:25.56,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Mousse. Where have you been?
Dialogue: 50,0:17:35.20,0:17:36.15,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,What if...
Dialogue: 50,0:17:36.15,0:17:39.33,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,What if you knew a single\Ntree was tainted by poison?
Dialogue: 50,0:17:39.33,0:17:43.21,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,{\q2}Poison that would contaminate the forest,\Nspreading from tree to tree.
Dialogue: 50,0:17:43.33,0:17:46.30,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,From tree to people,\Nand kill the island.
Dialogue: 50,0:17:46.30,0:17:49.05,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,What if you knew about it beforehand?
Dialogue: 50,0:17:49.62,0:17:50.83,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,What are you talking about?
Dialogue: 50,0:17:50.83,0:17:52.44,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Please tell us what you mean.
Dialogue: 50,0:17:52.44,0:17:53.98,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,If we had a choice.
Dialogue: 50,0:17:55.69,0:17:57.77,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,What would we do with that one tree?
Dialogue: 50,0:17:59.57,0:18:01.07,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,What would we do?
Dialogue: 50,0:18:03.57,0:18:05.49,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Father, listen.
Dialogue: 50,0:18:05.49,0:18:06.95,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You have to stop them.
Dialogue: 50,0:18:06.95,0:18:08.08,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You fool.
Dialogue: 50,0:18:08.08,0:18:09.66,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Don't you understand what they've done?
Dialogue: 50,0:18:09.69,0:18:13.03,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,We can't leave things this way!\NWe'll regret it forever!
Dialogue: 50,0:18:13.03,0:18:15.99,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You've finally made such a dear friend.
Dialogue: 50,0:18:15.99,0:18:18.45,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,And we owe them so much!
Dialogue: 50,0:18:18.55,0:18:21.43,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Father, we can't leave\Nthem hurting like this!
Dialogue: 50,0:18:21.43,0:18:23.43,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,What are you talking about?
Dialogue: 50,0:18:26.39,0:18:30.42,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,There is no excuse, but on the\Ncommodore's behalf, I must say this:
Dialogue: 50,0:18:30.42,0:18:34.55,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,Those woods were already dead\Nbefore we arrived on this island.
Dialogue: 50,0:18:34.55,0:18:38.55,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,The worst thing about Tree Fever\Nis that it also infects plant life.
Dialogue: 50,0:18:38.55,0:18:43.60,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,{\q2}Commodore Noland understood this,\Nand that was his reason for doing what he did.
Dialogue: 50,0:18:43.60,0:18:47.48,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,This is also why he pleaded with\Nyou without regard for his own life.
Dialogue: 50,0:18:49.89,0:18:52.68,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,From people to forest\Nand forest to people,
Dialogue: 50,0:18:52.68,0:18:59.01,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,{\q2}several small islands have been destroyed\Nin exactly the same way. Killed by fever.
Dialogue: 50,0:19:00.60,0:19:03.10,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,But there's nothing to worry about.
Dialogue: 50,0:19:03.10,0:19:07.03,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,Yesterday, we finished inspecting\Nthe rest of the forest.
Dialogue: 50,0:19:07.03,0:19:09.62,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry we cut down\Nyour forest without knowing.
Dialogue: 50,0:19:09.62,0:19:12.58,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,And I feel worse that we\Nnever explained why we did it.
Dialogue: 50,0:19:12.58,0:19:16.29,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,It's probably unforgivable\Neven with an explanation.
Dialogue: 50,0:19:16.29,0:19:21.20,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,But a botanist would never harm\Na forest without good reason.
Dialogue: 50,0:19:21.20,0:19:24.87,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,{\q2}Trust me, the commodore doesn't have\Nanything against gods or spirits.
Dialogue: 50,0:19:27.80,0:19:30.59,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,It's just that he\Nalways has to make a choice.
Dialogue: 50,0:19:30.59,0:19:33.26,Flashbacks-207-,,0,0,0,,And he always knows\Nwhat is most important.
Dialogue: 50,0:19:34.47,0:19:36.06,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,So...
Dialogue: 50,0:19:36.06,0:19:38.44,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,That means that they did all of\Nthat to try to help our people?
Dialogue: 50,0:19:43.48,0:19:44.61,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Father!
Dialogue: 50,0:19:47.62,0:19:49.42,Thoughts-207-,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, Noland!
Dialogue: 50,0:19:49.45,0:19:51.03,Thoughts-207-,,0,0,0,,Please don't leave yet!
Dialogue: 50,0:19:53.05,0:19:54.88,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Does everyone have everything?
Dialogue: 50,0:19:54.99,0:19:56.62,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Not everything.
Dialogue: 50,0:19:56.62,0:19:58.96,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,You wuss, hah!
Dialogue: 50,0:19:59.58,0:20:01.54,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,All right, everyone, to your positions.
Dialogue: 50,0:20:01.54,0:20:02.96,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,It's time to set sail!
Dialogue: 50,0:20:02.96,0:20:05.46,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,We're now on our way back\Nto the Lvneel Kingdom!
Dialogue: 50,0:20:05.46,0:20:06.54,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,{\q2}– Yeah!\N– Yeah!
Dialogue: 50,0:20:08.15,0:20:10.61,Thoughts-207-,,0,0,0,,Noland!
Dialogue: 50,0:20:11.31,0:20:14.31,Thoughts-207-,,0,0,0,,I can't believe I made such a mistake!
Dialogue: 50,0:20:14.31,0:20:16.23,Thoughts-207-,,0,0,0,,Noland! Wait!
Dialogue: 50,0:20:19.65,0:20:21.48,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Set sail!
Dialogue: 50,0:20:30.02,0:20:31.81,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,The bell.
Dialogue: 50,0:20:31.81,0:20:33.61,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Why would it be ringing now?
Dialogue: 50,0:20:33.61,0:20:36.56,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,– Ring it!
Dialogue: 50,0:20:36.56,0:20:38.61,Thoughts-207-,,0,0,0,,I'm so sorry, Noland!
Dialogue: 50,0:20:39.44,0:20:40.82,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Ring louder!
Dialogue: 50,0:20:40.82,0:20:43.07,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Noland and the rest\Nof them can't hear you!
Dialogue: 50,0:20:46.12,0:20:47.66,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Look over there!
Dialogue: 50,0:20:57.29,0:20:59.21,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Wait! Noland!
Dialogue: 50,0:21:00.92,0:21:02.80,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Is that you, Kalgara?
Dialogue: 50,0:21:17.85,0:21:19.56,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Come back!
Dialogue: 50,0:21:24.05,0:21:25.89,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Noland!
Dialogue: 50,0:21:26.17,0:21:28.84,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Come back, please, Noland!\NYou've got to!
Dialogue: 50,0:21:30.76,0:21:34.01,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I'll ring the bell so you\Ncan find your way back to us!
Dialogue: 50,0:21:34.01,0:21:36.68,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I don't want you to\Nlose sight of this island!
Dialogue: 50,0:21:36.68,0:21:39.27,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Because... one day...
Dialogue: 50,0:21:39.27,0:21:42.73,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I want you to return, my dear friend.
Dialogue: 50,0:21:42.73,0:21:44.50,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Noland!
Dialogue: 50,0:21:44.50,0:21:46.29,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Please come back!
Dialogue: 50,0:21:56.59,0:21:59.97,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I know we'll meet\Nagain someday, Noland.
Dialogue: 50,0:21:59.97,0:22:01.81,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Have a safe voyage.
Dialogue: 50,0:22:04.90,0:22:08.11,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,So... I can come back again?
Dialogue: 50,0:22:12.94,0:22:15.52,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Of course I will. I'll come back.
Dialogue: 50,0:22:20.45,0:22:22.15,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,Someday, Kalgara!
Dialogue: 50,0:22:22.15,0:22:24.65,Main-207-,,0,0,0,,I know we'll meet\Nagain someday, Noland.
Comment: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:00.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{=3}===============================DIALOGUE============================
